<ns0:exercise xmlns:ns0="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:ns1="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="fs-id1167836409564" class="material-set-2">
<ns0:problem id="fs-id1167836409567">
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167836553948">Atsushi he needs to exercise enough to burn 600 calories each day. He prefers to either run or bike and burns 20 calories per minute while running and 15 calories a minute while biking.</ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167836553953"><ns0:span class="token">ⓐ</ns0:span> If <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">x</ns0:emphasis> is the number of minutes that Atsushi runs and <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">y</ns0:emphasis> is the number minutes he bikes, find the inequality that models the situation.<ns0:newline />
<ns0:span class="token">ⓑ</ns0:span> Graph the inequality.<ns0:newline />
<ns0:span class="token">ⓒ</ns0:span> List three solutions to the inequality. What options do the solutions provide Atsushi?</ns0:para>
</ns0:problem>
<ns0:solution id="fs-id1167829704678">
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167829704681"><ns0:span class="token">ⓐ</ns0:span> <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mn>20</ns1:mn><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>15</ns1:mn><ns1:mi>y</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>≥</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>600</ns1:mn></ns1:mrow></ns1:math><ns0:newline />
<ns0:span class="token">ⓑ</ns0:span> <ns0:newline />
<ns0:media id="fs-id1167829594005" alt="The figure has a straight line graphed on the x y-coordinate plane. The x-axis runs from 0 to 50. The y-axis runs from 0 to 50. The line goes through the points (0, 40) and (30, 0). The line divides the coordinate plane into two halves. The top right half and the line are colored red to indicate that this is the solution set.">
